WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:07.100
We now know that there are no legally valid
or historically valid reasons to prevent Donald

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:11.950
Trump's former national security advisor,
the non indicted one John Bolton from testifying

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:13.780
in the Senate impeachment trial.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:20.240
We suspect that there are at least a couple
of Republican votes in favor of John Bolton

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:21.240
testifying.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:24.230
We don't yet know whether there will be 51
total votes.

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:29.510
Republicans are absolutely panicking that
the testimony that John Bolton might give

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:35.120
could quote open the floodgates according
to Republican sources who spoke to Axios yesterday.

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:37.970
I told you that in John Bolton's upcoming
book.

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:43.390
He just says, Trump personally told me withhold
the aid to Ukraine until Ukraine smears Joe

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:45.160
Biden publicly.

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:51.989
So when you hear from different, uh, Trump
attorneys speculating that there was not conditionality,

00:00:51.989 --> 00:00:55.670
that there was not pressure or whatever, and
that they have no firsthand witnesses saying

00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:58.570
otherwise, John Bolton would be such a firsthand
witness.

00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:04.269
He would say, presumably if he tells the same
story that he tells in his book, a boy Trump

00:01:04.269 --> 00:01:10.130
came to me and said, uh, hold the aid until
we get these, uh, investigation announcements.

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:15.580
Republicans have said endlessly, they want
firsthand sources, but they are working to

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:19.060
block a firsthand source like John Bolton.

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:23.580
So first and foremost is the question of whether
four Republican senators will vote to bring

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:25.080
Bolton into testify.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:27.380
We dealt with that in the last segment.

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:33.189
Then there is part two of this Axios is reporting
that Republican sources tell them party leaders

00:01:33.189 --> 00:01:39.119
and the white house are going to try to resist
witnesses altogether, including Bolton because

00:01:39.119 --> 00:01:44.229
as one aid put it quote, there is a sense
in the Senate that if one witness is allowed,

00:01:44.229 --> 00:01:45.829
the floodgates are open.

00:01:45.829 --> 00:01:51.549
If Bolton says stuff that implicates, say,
Mick Mulvaney or Mike Pompeo, then calls for

00:01:51.549 --> 00:01:56.020
them to testify will intensify as they should.

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:57.560
That is exactly right.

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:02.610
What arguments will Republicans make against
the testimony of Bolton when it comes up?

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:04.000
There's going to be a few things.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:06.990
One, we already heard, I played a clip earlier
of Senator John Barrasso.

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:09.609
They will say, you know, we're, we're doing
a lot here.

00:02:09.609 --> 00:02:14.819
We've got 24 hours on one side, 24 hours from
the other side, 16 hours of questions.

00:02:14.819 --> 00:02:16.189
We'll decide later.

00:02:16.189 --> 00:02:20.819
Do we really need to hear more stuff in general,
making the argument that just looking at the

00:02:20.819 --> 00:02:25.129
clock like just the number of hours that they've,
they've done this would suggest they don't

00:02:25.129 --> 00:02:26.239
need to hear from witnesses.

00:02:26.239 --> 00:02:27.239
That's a fact.

00:02:27.239 --> 00:02:28.980
Free assessment.

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:33.579
They will argue that what Bolton has to say
won't change the primary facts.

00:02:33.579 --> 00:02:35.329
Now of course that's not true.

00:02:35.329 --> 00:02:40.879
John Bolton would be a firsthand witnesses
witness who would be able to testify personally.

00:02:40.879 --> 00:02:45.530
Trump told me withhold the aide until they
announced the investigations.

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:52.029
They will say the aid which was paused, not
withheld, was ultimately released and nobody

00:02:52.029 --> 00:02:54.059
ended up publicly smearing Joe Biden.

00:02:54.059 --> 00:02:59.750
Now of course that happened because they got
caught and they scrambled to clean it up,

00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:02.189
but Republicans will still use that as an
argument.

00:03:02.189 --> 00:03:07.659
They will say the Ukrainian president has
said there was no pressure on him to announce

00:03:07.659 --> 00:03:12.379
these investigations and that the phone call
didn't mention a specific quid pro quo.

00:03:12.379 --> 00:03:13.859
So we don't need to hear from John Bolton.

00:03:13.859 --> 00:03:17.890
Of course, John Bolton would still be a firsthand
witness who could tell us exactly what Trump

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:21.760
said, but that also ignores how politics works,
right?

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:27.150
These things aren't made explicit and phone
calls between the CEOs or the presidents.

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:34.939
It is all discussed and pushed behind the
scenes by people like Rudy, Giuliani and others.

00:03:34.939 --> 00:03:39.159
Now, of course, every single one of those
talking points is easily debunked bubble and

00:03:39.159 --> 00:03:42.870
it runs directly counter to the Republican
complaints about we run.

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:47.349
We want firsthand witnesses and we don't have
them, but they are still going to make the

00:03:47.349 --> 00:03:52.689
strongest case possible to prevent Bolton
from testifying because they know it would

00:03:52.689 --> 00:03:53.930
